# A peer block with no `family` section: the OPEN and the End-of-RIB, as hex.
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 4724 Section 4 -- "The End-of-RIB marker MUST be sent by a BGP
#            speaker to its peer once it completes the initial routing update
#            (including the case when there is no update to send) for an address
#            family after the BGP session is established". This peer declares no
#            family, so it advertises no Multiprotocol capability, and ze-peer
#            mirrors the OPEN it receives and advertises none either. RFC 4271
#            carries IPv4 unicast without a capability, so the session exchanges
#            it and the marker is owed for it.
# PREVENTS:  the silent skip. Before the fix in capability.Negotiate, both sides
#            contributed the empty set to the family intersection, the End-of-RIB
#            loop in sendInitialRoutes never ran, and nothing logged or counted
#            the absence: the peer waited forever for a barrier that never came.
#
# The OPEN assertion is the other half, and it is what AC-2 turns on: the fix is
# in the NEGOTIATION, not in the OPEN builder, so ze still advertises no
# Multiprotocol capability here. A fix that synthesized one would change these
# bytes for every peer configured this way.
#
# seq=1, the OPEN, field by field: 16 marker octets, length 0x0025 = 37, type 01 =
# OPEN, version 04, My AS 0xFDE8 = 65000, Hold Time 0x005A = 90, BGP Identifier
# 01020304 = 1.2.3.4, Optional Parameters Length 0x08, then one type-2 parameter
# of 6 bytes carrying ASN4 alone (code 0x41, length 04, AS 0x0000FDE8). No
# capability code 01. 19+10+8 = 37.
#
# seq=2, the marker: an UPDATE message with the minimum length (RFC 4724 Section
# 2) -- length 0x0017 = 23, type 02, withdrawn-routes-length 0x0000,
# path-attribute-length 0x0000.

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=open:value=inspect-open-message
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00250104FDE8005A0102030408020641040000FDE8
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=2:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65000
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=10s
